🌲 prove.play-await-reads-three-answers

## --help
rc=0
usage:
  rhx git.grove.play.await grove-1 --play <name>               # ✔ accurate — names the play, an answer
  rhx git.grove.play.await grove-1 --play <name> --within 3600 # a longer bound
  rhx git.grove.play.await grove-1 --play <name> --lines 80    # how much tail to print
  rhx git.grove.play.await grove-1 --play <name> --quiet       # exit code only; errors still print
  rhx git.grove.play.await --grove grove-2 --play <name>       # --grove still works
  rhx git.grove.play.await grove-1                             # 🌙 coarse — names no play, a guess

guarantee:
  - READ-ONLY on the grove. per poll, with `--play`, it runs two ssh asks — a
    reachability `true`, then one `pgrep` — and without it, one pane read. it
    types no key into the pane and changes no state
  - BOUNDED. `--within` caps the polls, each ssh is capped at 30s, and a
    malformed flag refuses at once rather than loop
  - it prints ONE progress line per state CHANGE, so a long wait is legible

exit:
  0 = a verdict: the play finished (or, coarse, the pane is back at a non-bash
      shell); tail printed
  1 = a malfunction: the grove could not be asked, or this checkout lacks the
      ductwork the ask rides on — either way, no state was observed
  2 = the call was malformed — an absent value, an unknown flag, two groves
  3 = no verdict: `--within` elapsed with the play still busy, or the coarse
      read saw `bash` and cannot tell done from busy. the tail is printed anyway

## a value flag with no value
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: git.grove.play.await: --play needs a value
   fix: rhx git.grove.play.await <grove> --play <name> --within 600

## a zero interval
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: git.grove.play.await: --every must be a whole number of seconds ≥ 1, got '0'
   fix: rhx git.grove.play.await <grove> --play <name> --every 15 --within 600

## two groves named
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: git.grove.play.await: two groves named: 'grove-1' and 'grove-2'
   fix: rhx git.grove.play.await <grove> --play <name> --within 600

## a --grove and a bare grove
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: git.grove.play.await: two groves named: 'grove-1' and 'grove-2'
   fix: rhx git.grove.play.await <grove> --play <name> --within 600

## a --timeout, which is no flag
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: git.grove.play.await: unknown arg '--timeout'
   the bound is --within, in seconds — there is no --timeout
   fix: rhx git.grove.play.await <grove> --play <name> --within 600

## an unknown flag
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: git.grove.play.await: unknown arg '--wait'
   the flags are --grove --play --every --within --lines --quiet
   fix: rhx git.grove.play.await <grove> --play <name> --within 600

## --play · pgrep finds none → finished
rc=0
⏳ git.grove.play.await --grove grove-1 --every 15s --within 1800s
   ├─ duct: duct://grove-1/main/mechanic
   ├─ play: x.play.sh (matched by its filename)
   └─ waits for that play's process to exit

   ✔ the play finished after 0s

[stub] rhx git.grove.read grove-1 --lines 40

## --play · pgrep finds the play → bound hit
rc=3
⏳ git.grove.play.await --grove grove-1 --every 5s --within 2s
   ├─ duct: duct://grove-1/main/mechanic
   ├─ play: x.play.sh (matched by its filename)
   └─ waits for that play's process to exit

   • 0s — the play runs (pid 4242)

   🌙 still busy after 2s — the play may simply need longer
      ⇒ this is a bound, not a verdict: raise it with --within

[stub] rhx git.grove.read grove-1 --lines 40

## --play · --quiet → exit code only, no output
rc=0


## --play · --quiet, bound hit → rc 3, no output
rc=3


## --play · pgrep cannot be asked → no verdict
rc=1
⏳ git.grove.play.await --grove grove-1 --every 15s --within 1800s
   ├─ duct: duct://grove-1/main/mechanic
   ├─ play: x.play.sh (matched by its filename)
   └─ waits for that play's process to exit

   💥 MalfunctionError: the grove could not be asked whether the play runs
      ⇒ ssh, its time bound, or pgrep failed; that is no answer, so this
        refuses to call the play finished
      fix: rhx git.grove.wake grove-1, then await again

## --play · --quiet, cannot be asked → rc 1, the error still prints
rc=1
   💥 MalfunctionError: the grove could not be asked whether the play runs
      ⇒ ssh, its time bound, or pgrep failed; that is no answer, so this
        refuses to call the play finished
      fix: rhx git.grove.wake grove-1, then await again

## --play · the grove does not answer
rc=1
⏳ git.grove.play.await --grove grove-1 --every 15s --within 1800s
   ├─ duct: duct://grove-1/main/mechanic
   ├─ play: x.play.sh (matched by its filename)
   └─ waits for that play's process to exit

   💥 MalfunctionError: the grove did not answer, so the play's state is unknown
      ⇒ empty output from an unreachable box looks exactly like a
        finished play, so this refuses to guess between them
      fix: rhx git.grove.wake grove-1

