## coarse · pane at bash → a guess
rc=3
⏳ git.grove.play.await --grove grove-1 --every 15s --within 1800s
   ├─ duct: duct://grove-1/main/mechanic
   └─ waits for the pane to return to a shell

   🌙 no --play given, so this is the coarse read: a play runs as
      'bash <script>', and 'bash' is indistinguishable from an idle
      shell. it may report done while the play still runs.
      ⇒ for an accurate wait, name it: --play <name>

   🌙 the pane reports 'bash' after 0s — this may mean done,
      or a play still running, and this probe cannot tell them apart
      ⇒ re-run with --play <name> for an answer rather than a guess

